# RULE 12 — MODEL TIER POLICY (owner-locked 2026-08-03)

**Canonical prose:** `docs/specs/MODEL-TIER-POLICY.md` (same text). This rule is alwaysApply so every Cursor session autoloads it.

**Invariant:** Tier **never** weakens the proof bar. Cheap model output still needs ratcheting guard + (money) 3-gate + live verify. Cheaper ≠ weaker verification.

## The three tiers (by TASK, not by agent brand)

| Tier | Use for | Cursor product names (examples; verify current) |
|------|---------|--------------------------------------------------|
| **A — FRONTIER** | Financial cluster (`accounting.*` / `catalogs.accounts` / migrations / posting / GL / RLS), root-cause on money/false-green, architecture, audit completeness-discriminator reasoning, GUARD on money | Highest-capability available (e.g. Opus / GPT-frontier / Grok-high) |
| **B — WORKHORSE** | Well-specified non-financial features, guards/tests, wiring to a clear spec, **Program scoreboard**, non-trivial UI (e.g. Loans & Advances screens) | Sonnet-class / mid GPT-Grok |
| **C — FAST/CHEAP** | Mechanical class waves (MISSING-CREATOR, BOX-IN-BOX, CALENDAR/DATE, DEAD-CLICK, picker wiring against Cascade instance list), design-token/palette ratchet, docs, repetitive refactors | Composer / Cursor Auto |

## Cursor lane defaults (HARD)

| Work | Tier |
|------|------|
| Mechanical waves from Cascade cards (instance list + DRAIN_PROOF) | **C** |
| Real feature UI / scoreboard / non-trivial chrome logic | **B** |
| Anything that turns out to touch money, schema, RLS, migrations, or linkage law | **A** immediately |

Most UI volume is Tier C — that is where token savings come from. Do not run mechanical waves on Tier A.

## Other agents (defaults)

- **Cascade (auditor):** A/B — completeness discriminator is high-stakes; do not audit cheap.
- **Claude Coder (money):** **A** always.
- **GUARD (verifier):** **A** on money / false-green samples; never cheap the net.

## Escalation (one-way toward safety)

1. Start at the tier the task type dictates.
2. **Stuck** (2 red CI cycles / can't root-cause / fix looks wrong) → escalate **one tier up** — do not grind.
3. Mechanical work that hides money/logic → **jump to A**.
4. **Never down-tier** a financial/migration task to save tokens.
5. Unproven / trial models: throwaway mechanical only until they hold the guard bar.

## Subagents

When spawning Task/subagents: pick `model` by this table. Do not run financial/migration design on Tier C.

## Tie-breakers

Tokens < trust · cheap < correct · grind on C < escalate · memory < this file + `docs/specs/MODEL-TIER-POLICY.md`.
